   "key": "func PoincarePlotView.beatPairs()",
   "hash": "0b2991d81edcc237",
   "does": "Returns consecutive (RR_i, RR_i+1) pairs in ms within [windowStart, min(windowEnd, points.count)), skipping a pair if either beat is flagged artifact (beats beyond flags array count as clean).",
   "entry": null,
   "calls": [],
   "reads": [],
   "writes": [],
   "branches": [
    {
     "at": "+1",
     "cond": "session.rrSeries is nil",
     "effect": "returns [] (plot blank)"
    },
    {
     "at": "+2",
     "cond": "session.artifactFlags ?? []",
     "effect": "nil flags treated as no artifacts — every beat counts as clean"
    },
    {
     "at": "+5",
     "cond": "windowStart >= 0 and windowEnd > windowStart+1",
     "effect": "false → returns [] (prevents 0..<-1 range trap); true → iterates pairs"
    },
    {
     "at": "+7",
     "cond": "i < flags.count",
     "effect": "true → reads flags[i].isArtifact; false → beat treated as not artifact"
    },
    {
     "at": "+8",
     "cond": "i+1 < flags.count",
     "effect": "true → reads flags[i+1].isArtifact; false → not artifact"
    },
    {
     "at": "+9",
     "cond": "either beat is artifact",
     "effect": "pair dropped (nil); else pair returned"
    }
   ],
   "flags": [
    {
     "kind": "duplicate",
     "sev": "med",
     "text": "Poincaré pair extraction exists three times with different rules: here beats beyond artifactFlags.count (incl. artifactFlags == nil) count as clean; the PDF renderer's isCleanPair returns false when i or i+1 >= flags.count, so a session with nil/short flags (SessionMerger sets artifactFlags = nil after a merge, SessionMerger.swift:349) gets an empty PDF Poincaré plot while the app plots every beat; HRVDetailV2View.buildPoincarePairs uses the whole series with no window and no artifact filter. Padding also differs (15% here vs 10% in PDF PoincareScale).",
